  "summary": "Possible typosquat of @solana/spl-token under @solana-labs scope",
  "details": "Package name `@solana-labs/spl-toke` is a one-character truncation of the well-known `@solana/spl-token` library and is published under a scope (`@solana-labs`) that mimics the official Solana Labs organization. Static patterns matched on keyword co-occurrence in the minified bundles (`lib/index.cjs.js`, `lib/index.esm.js`) — `require('child_process')`, `fetch(`, `https.get`, and `POST`/`GET` literals appear in proximity — but these are typical of an SPL-token-style bundle that includes RPC client code and utility helpers, and traced-code corroboration of an exfiltration path is not available. The combination of (a) a confusable name targeting a top-tier Solana ecosystem package and (b) suspicious primitives in the shipped bundle warrants human review of intent before allowing installation.",
